=== Phase 05 — profile data layer: measurement transcript ===

The repo has no unit-test runner (`package.json` scripts: dev/build/start/lint/typecheck/
test:e2e/db:types), and adding one is a package.json change outside this phase's ownership.
So the REAL modules were compiled to CJS and exercised against the REAL local Supabase over
HTTP — stronger than phase 04's pure-function transcript, because every number below came
back through PostgREST and `public.kudos_readable`, not from a fabricated row object.

How it was built and run (scratchpad only; nothing under plans/ is a .js file, which is what
turned `npm run lint` red in phase 04):

  npx tsc -p <scratchpad>/tsconfig.harness.json      # rootDir = repo root, paths { "@/*": ["./*"] }
    files: lib/profile/{profile-queries,profile-data}.ts
           lib/kudos/{queries,map-kudos-card,derive,viewer}.ts
           app/profile/_actions/fetch-profile-kudos-page.ts
  find <out> -name '*.js' -exec sed -i 's|require("@/|require("<out>/|g' {} +
  # ONE substitution, and only one: `@/lib/supabase/server`'s createClient, whose `cookies()`
  # needs a Next request scope. The action module itself is the real compiled file, so its
  # validation branches, its `resolveViewer()` call and its column choice are all real.
  sed -i 's|require("<out>/lib/supabase/server")|require("<scratchpad>/server-stub")|g' <out>/app/profile/_actions/*.js

Sessions are real: `POST /auth/v1/signup` through supabase-js, and the SEC_002 author composes
through F005's real `create_kudos()` RPC. Ground truth is read as superuser via
`docker exec supabase_db_my-app psql` (psql is not on PATH in this WSL environment).

DATABASE STATE: `npx supabase db reset` was run BEFORE any measurement (exit 0, all three
migrations applied, seed loaded), verified at
`kudos=58 anon=1 auth_users=0 linked=0`. Obligation D from phase 04's handover: F005's compose
e2e had left `sunners.id = 10` linked to a real auth user, so the database was NOT in seed
state; it is now, and every number below is reproducible from a reset.

