==============================================================================
== PART 3 — the seed has NO duplicate sent_at at all
==============================================================================
This is why PART 2's tie rows had to be constructed. Measured on the reset database:

  select sent_at, count(*) from public.kudos group by 1 having count(*) > 1;
 sent_at | count 
---------+-------
(0 rows)

The phase file's Key Insight 1 says 'the seed generates many' equal sent_at values.
It does not generate any. So a keyset proof over seed data alone CANNOT distinguish the
correct predicate from the degraded `sent_at.lt`-only form — hence M1a-M1e above.

